  "content": "<p><a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/news/orionid-meteor-shower-uk-dates-times-b3059811.html#main-content\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Skip to content</a></p><ol><li><a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">All</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/news\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">News</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/sport\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Sport</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/culture\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Culture</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/lifestyle\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Lifestyle</a></li></ol>\n\n<figure><p><img src=\"https://static.independent.co.uk/2022/10/21/09/7907141b6916cd43d1f189a9c46ff4ebY29udGVudHNlYXJjaGFwaSwxNjY2NDI3MDQ0-2.17306523.jpg\" alt=\"The Orionid meteor is expected to peak on October 21\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" /></p><figcaption>The Orionid meteor is expected to peak on October 21 (PA Archive)</figcaption></figure><ul><li>The Orionid meteor shower is visible in the night sky from 2 October until 7 November, reaching its peak on 21 October. </li><li>The meteors are debris left behind by Halley's Comet, which vapourise upon entering <a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/topic/earth\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Earth</a>'s atmosphere to create visible streaks of light. </li><li>Stargazers can view the shower by looking up in dark areas, though a waxing gibbous <a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/topic/moon\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Moon</a> may make dimmer meteors harder to spot this year. </li><li>Named after the constellation <a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/topic/orion\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Orion</a> from where they appear to originate, the meteors can be seen across the entire night sky. </li><li>Halley's Comet, officially known as 1P/Halley, is also responsible for the Eta Aquariids meteor shower that occurs every May. </li></ul><figure><figcaption>In full</figcaption><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/space/orionid-meteor-shower-sky-when-this-week-b3059779.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><h3>Orionid meteor shower will light up UK skies this week. Here’s when to see it</h3><p><img src=\"https://static.independent.co.uk/2024/10/21/09/orionids-meteor-shower-peak-tonight.jpg?quality=75&amp;width=83&amp;auto=webp%2083w\" alt=\"Orionid meteor shower will light up UK skies this week. Here’s when to see it\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" /></p></a></li></ul></figure><p>More bulletins</p><h3>Thank you for registering</h3><p>Please refresh the page or navigate to another page on the site to be automatically logged inPlease refresh your browser to be logged in</p>"
